      "name": "InitializeDataTables",
      "signature": "void InitializeDataTables(dword * pdwSource)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes data tables by copying source data and dereferencing pointer array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy first 0x48 (72) dwords from source to g_pInitialDataBlock\n2. Store source pointer to g_pSourceData\n3. Iterate through g_ppPtrTable, dereferencing each pointer\n4. Copy 0x40 (64) dwords from each dereferenced pointer to g_pOutputBuffer\n\nParameters:\n- pdwSource (dword*): Pointer to source data block (72 dwords)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x48 (72): Size of initial data block in dwords\n- 0x40 (64): Size of each table entry in dwords\n- 0x6fab1500: End of pointer table (0x6fab143c + 0xC4 bytes)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
