      "name": "RenderTileLineWithBlend",
      "signature": "void RenderTileLineWithBlend(int nXOffset, int nYOffset, byte * pbSourceLine, int nXPos, int nYPos, int nXDelta, int nYDelta, int nXInc, int nYInc, byte byShift)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders a tile line with alpha blending using a lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate blend lookup table offset from X/Y positions shifted by byShift\n2. Iterate through nYInc scan lines of the tile\n3. For each line, read run-length encoded source data (skip count, pixel count)\n4. Skip lines outside screen bounds or empty runs\n5. Calculate clipping against screen left (g_nClipLeft) and right (g_nClipRight) bounds\n6. Use Duff's device (computed goto) to process 1-32 pixels per iteration\n7. For each pixel: blend = g_abBlendLookup[(srcPixel << 8) + dstPixel]\n\nParameters:\n  nXOffset     - IMPLICIT ECX: Base X offset for destination\n  nYOffset     - IMPLICIT EDX: Base Y offset for destination\n  pbSourceLine - Pointer to RLE-compressed source line data\n  nXPos        - Current X position in tile space\n  nYPos        - Current Y position in tile space\n  nXDelta      - Delta X for perspective calculation\n  nYDelta      - Delta Y for perspective calculation\n  nXInc        - X increment per scan line\n  nYInc        - Number of scan lines to render\n  byShift      - Bit shift for coordinate to lookup table mapping\n\nReturns:\n  void - Renders directly to screen buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if nYInc <= 0 (no lines to render)\n  - Lines skipped if outside vertical clip bounds\n  - Clipped horizontally against g_nClipLeft (0x6fab465c) and g_nClipRight (0x6fabd204)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x6fab51e4  - g_abTileBlendLUT: Tile blend lookup table (32x32 entries)\n  0x6fab1550  - g_abBlendLookup: 256x256 alpha blend lookup table\n  0x6fab1424  - g_dwScreenPitch: Screen buffer pitch (bytes per row)\n  0x6fab465c  - g_nClipLeft: Left clipping boundary\n  0x6fabd204  - g_nClipRight: Right clipping boundary\n  0x6fabd1e4  - g_nClipBottom: Bottom clipping boundary (max visible pixels)\n  0x6fab4668  - g_nClipTop: Top clipping boundary\n\nDuff's Device:\n  Jump table at 0x6faa24e8 handles 1-32 pixels with unrolled loop\n  Entry (nPixelCount-1) jumps to code processing that many pixels",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d545c3bdced40cdd6e9e80d64d15a8741afef46a49c2d411da9128e90c00214e",
