      "name": "InitializeStrideOffsetTable",
      "signature": "void InitializeStrideOffsetTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize stride offset lookup table with negated stride multipliers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global stride increment value\n2. Calculate initial offset as -stride * 32 (0x20)\n3. Fill table starting at g_adStrideOffsetTable with computed offsets\n4. Increment offset by stride for each entry\n5. Continue until reaching table boundary at 0x6fab51e0\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwStrideIncrement global contains stride value\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Table stride: 4 bytes per entry (DWORD array)\n- Offset increment: stride value\n- Used for accelerating stride-based rendering calculations",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
