      "name": "RenderTileLineNormal",
      "signature": "void RenderTileLineNormal(void * pRenderState, dword dwYOffset, dword dwScreenX, dword dwScreenY, dword * pdwTileCoords)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Render tile scanline without special alpha blending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract tile coordinate deltas from pdwTileCoords array\n2. Shift coordinates left by 4 bits for 16-bit fixed-point calculation\n3. Check pRenderState flags byte for alpha blend flag (0x4)\n4. If not alpha blending: iterate through visible scanlines\n5. Clip scanline to screen bounds using global width/height tables\n6. Fetch source data offset and blend lookup values\n7. Render pixels with palette lookup (output_buffer + blend*256)\n8. If alpha blending: delegate to RenderTileLineWithBlend helper\n\nParameters:\n- pRenderState (void*): Render context struct (flags at +8, data ptr at +0x10)\n- dwYOffset (dword): Y coordinate (ECX __fastcall)\n- dwScreenX (dword): Screen X origin (EDX __fastcall)\n- dwScreenY (dword): Screen Y origin (Stack[0x4])\n- pdwTileCoords (dword*): [TileX, TileY, TileEndX, TileEndY]\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Alpha blend flag in pRenderState->flags byte\n- 0x20: Blend lookup stride (32 bytes per scanline)\n- 0x100: Output palette lookup multiplier (256 colors)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:2d4939bba6e3f0db4624370ca57430ce7d1fa7b30214164af3221811175bed58",
