      "name": "SetColorDepth",
      "signature": "void SetColorDepth(uint dwColorDepth)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "SetColorDepth - Sets the global color depth value for graphics rendering.\n\nThis function stores the requested color depth to g_nColorDepth, but only\nif the current video mode (g_nVideoMode) supports color depth configuration.\nVideo modes below 4 do not support custom color depth and will clear the value to 0.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read g_nVideoMode from global storage\n2. Compare video mode against threshold (4)\n3. If mode < 4: Set g_nColorDepth to 0 (unsupported mode)\n4. If mode >= 4: Set g_nColorDepth to dwColorDepth parameter\n\nParameters:\n  dwColorDepth (uint) - Requested color depth in bits per pixel (e.g., 8, 16, 24, 32)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; result stored in g_nColorDepth global\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Video mode 0-3: Color depth is forced to 0 regardless of parameter\n  - Video mode 4+: Color depth is set to the requested value\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nColorDepth (0x6faae194) - Stores the active color depth setting\n\nGlobals Read:\n  g_nVideoMode (0x6fabd228) - Current video/display mode (threshold: 4)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:9a845f44f5e1e896da124184012dc5ec93f9b129fef48ad44369b002dde8cc98",
