      "name": "IncrementFrameIndex",
      "signature": "void IncrementFrameIndex(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Increments the frame index by 0x20 and caps it at 0x200.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current frame index from g_dwCurrentFrameIndex\n2. Check if index is below cap (0x200)\n3. If below cap, increment by 0x20\n4. If new value exceeds or equals cap, set to cap (0x200)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwCurrentFrameIndex modified as side effect\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x200 (512): Maximum frame index value (cap)\n- 0x20 (32): Frame index increment step",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4d68cc005dd4196e8a385c701dd070312f890f9f9b6aca7aff0e232d6d698d56",
