      "name": "ValidateCoordinateRange",
      "signature": "bool ValidateCoordinateRange(int nX, int nY)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates that coordinates are within acceptable range of viewport boundaries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert video mode is valid (4, 5, 6, or 7)\n2. Assert perspective mode is enabled\n3. Calculate absolute distance from nX to global X reference\n4. Return false if distance exceeds 0x320000\n5. Calculate absolute distance from nY to global Y reference\n6. Return true if both distances within threshold, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- nX (int): X coordinate to validate\n- nY (int): Y coordinate to validate\n\nReturns:\n- true if both coordinates within 0x320000 of viewport origin\n- false if either coordinate exceeds threshold\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x320000 (3276800): Maximum valid coordinate offset from viewport center",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d83f18ade646fe00e45a003b9110f130b48eb85fab4e2336be54bf525571ee11",
