      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases a graphics subsurface via virtual function callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load graphics interface pointer from g_pGfxInterface\n2. Calculate offset address from first parameter with LEA\n3. Invoke virtual function at offset 0x90 with calculated offset\n4. Return with 3 arguments cleaned up by caller\n\nParameters:\n- pdwBuffer (dword*): Surface data buffer or handle\n- nWidth (dword): Width or stride value\n- nHeight (dword): Height or surface identifier\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNote:\n- __stdcall calling convention (caller cleans 12 bytes)\n- Calls virtual function; no return value used",
