      "name": "InsertLinkedListNode",
      "signature": "void InsertLinkedListNode(void * this, int param_1, int param_2, int param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Insert node into linked list container by type and priority offset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check nNode parameter: if 0, use default offset (this + 4); else compute position = *this + nNode\n2. Validate target position contains valid data; if occupied, call FUN_6fb997be for validation\n3. Check nPriority parameter: if 0, use default (this + 4); else compute list base = *this + nPriority\n4. Load nListType from stack parameter\n5. If nListType == 1: Insert as head node (copy existing pointers, create new bidirectional links)\n6. Else: Insert at calculated position in middle/tail of list\n7. Handle negative offset adjustments for backwards pointer arithmetic using NOT and SUB\n8. Store final node reference and update target back link\n\nParameters:\n  this: GameDataList* via __thiscall ECX (implicit), list container structure\n  nNode: Offset into structure or node identifier (0=default offset 4)\n  nListType: Insertion mode (1=head insert, else=position insert)\n  nPriority: Priority/position adjustment offset (0=default offset 4)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates linked list structure in place; no return value",
