      "name": "ExceptionHandler_UnpackContext",
      "signature": "void ExceptionHandler_UnpackContext(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord, PVOID pContextData, DWORD dwExceptionCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exception handler that unpacks context data and invokes exception processing routine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load context data structure pointer from second parameter (pContextData)\n2. Extract field at offset 0xc (exception-specific data)\n3. Extract field at offset 0x8 (pointer to pointer, dereferenced for parameter)\n4. Extract field at offset 0x10 (additional context value)\n5. Call FUN_6fb9b884 with unpacked fields and original context pointer\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord: Exception record from OS\n- PVOID pContextData: Pointer to context structure containing:\n  - [0x8]: Pointer to pointer (nested data reference)\n  - [0xc]: Exception-specific data block\n  - [0x10]: Additional context value\n- DWORD dwExceptionCode: Exception code/type identifier\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- All context fields extracted as raw pointers/values before passing downstream\n- Exception record passed through unchanged to FUN_6fb9b884\n- Null terminator (0x00) passed as last parameter to called function",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
