      "comment": "Cleanup and optionally delete object instance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fb99cc6() with this pointer to perform cleanup operations on the object instance\n2. Test if destruction flag (bDestructFlag) has low bit (0x01) set\n3. If (bDestructFlag & 0x01) is non-zero, call SafeDelete(this) to deallocate memory\n4. Return the object pointer in EAX (unchanged)\n\nParameters:\nthis (IMPLICIT, void*) - Pointer to object instance, passed in ECX (__thiscall convention)\nbDestructFlag (byte) - Control flag; if (bDestructFlag & 0x01) != 0, memory is deallocated after cleanup\n\nReturns:\nvoid* - Pointer to object instance (same as input this pointer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If bDestructFlag has bit 0 clear, cleanup occurs but memory is NOT freed\n- SafeDelete handles null pointers safely without error",
