      "name": "AllocateMemoryWithCache",
      "signature": "LPVOID AllocateMemoryWithCache(uint param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "LPVOID",
      "comment": "Allocates memory using cached descriptor blocks or falls back to heap allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If requested size <= g_dwMemoryBlockThreshold, attempt cached allocation\n2. Acquire critical section 9 to protect cache access\n3. Call AllocateMemoryDescriptorBlock to get cached memory\n4. Release critical section 9\n5. If cached allocation succeeded, return the block\n6. Fall back to HeapAlloc with 16-byte aligned size\n7. Return allocated memory pointer (or NULL on failure)\n\nParameters:\n  dwSize - Number of bytes to allocate\n\nReturns:\n  LPVOID - Pointer to allocated memory block, or NULL if allocation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero-size requests are treated as 1-byte allocations\n  - Heap allocations are rounded up to 16-byte boundary ((size + 15) & 0xFFFFFFF0)\n  - Critical section 9 protects the memory descriptor cache\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x9 - Critical section index for memory cache\n  0xF / 0xFFFFFFF0 - 16-byte alignment mask",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:6961861d3bd7aefc5f0dc62d0e39f3a7c4f46cf3320a5c22ab0f569a35d0aa7b",
