      "name": "SetupStructuredExceptionHandler",
      "signature": "void SetupStructuredExceptionHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Install structured exception handler (SEH) frame for thread-local exception handling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH frame with exception handler address and label pointers\n2. Save previous exception list from FS:[0] into stack\n3. Update FS:[0] to point to new SEH frame on stack\n4. Call GetOrCreateTlsContext() to retrieve thread-local context\n5. Check if handler function pointer is set at offset 0x60 in TLS context\n6. If handler exists, set SEH marker to 1 and invoke handler callback\n7. Set SEH marker to 0xFFFFFFFF for cleanup state\n8. Call FUN_6fba1655() for exception processing cleanup\n9. Return with restored exception chain\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function, uses thread-local storage)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses __stdcall calling convention for Windows SEH compatibility\n  - Exception list chaining through FS:[0] (Windows x86 standard)\n  - TLS context obtained via GetOrCreateTlsContext() if not cached\n  - Handler callback invocation through function pointer at offset 0x60\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x60 - Offset of handler function pointer in TLS context (relative to context base)\n  0x18 - Offset for SEH frame pointer storage in stack setup\n  0xFFFFFFFF - Sentinel value marking exception processing completion\n  FS:[0x0] - Thread exception list head (Windows x86 TEB standard)",
