      "name": "SetupExceptionHandler",
      "signature": "void SetupExceptionHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Setup C++ exception handler chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EBP and create stack frame for local variables\n2. Initialize exception state flag to -1 (error marker)\n3. Push exception frame pointer (g_pExceptionFrameInfo) onto stack\n4. Push handler address label (0x6fba138c) onto stack\n5. Save current FS:[0] thread exception list entry\n6. Link current stack frame into exception chain: FS:[0] = ESP\n7. Check if callback function PTR_FUN_6fbd9134 is non-NULL\n8. If callback exists: set dwExceptionState=1, call callback via indirect call\n9. If no callback or callback returned: set dwExceptionState=0xFFFFFFFF\n10. Call FUN_6fb9c278 to restore exception handler chain\n11. Pop registers and return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  (none - uses global exception handler callback pointer at 0x6fbd9134)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Exception state tracking: 0xFFFFFFFF (cleanup), 0x1 (callback executing), 0x0 (init)\n  Callback may be NULL - execution continues regardless\n  Function modifies thread's FS:[0] exception chain",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
