      "name": "ProcessLocaleStrings",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessLocaleStrings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates and processes locale/country code strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if locale code (g_szLocaleCode) is exactly 3 characters\n  2. Check if country code (g_szCountryCode) is exactly 3 characters\n  3. If locale code is not 3 chars, look up locale ID via FUN_00409d00\n  4. Otherwise set country ID to 0x2 (predefined value)\n  5. Enumerate system locales via callback FUN_004096d6 with flag 0x1\n  6. Validate locale flags: check bits 0x100, 0x200, and 0x7 mask\n  7. Clear validation flags if any required bit is missing\n\nParameters:\n  (none - no parameters, operates on global state)\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies global state (g_bLocaleIs3Char, g_bCountryIs3Char, \n    g_dwLocaleId, g_dwCountryId, g_dwLocaleValidation)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If locale code is exactly 3 chars, country ID is set to 0x2\n  - If locale code is not 3 chars, actual ID is looked up\n  - Validation fails if bits 0x100 OR 0x200 OR 0x7 mask are zero\n  - On validation failure, clears all bits in g_dwLocaleValidation",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:9d28e393a75234ddb76569eaaf36df1371c6b8c316f38c3c0982d3487afb7a18",
