      "name": "ValidateLocaleAndStoreId",
      "signature": "uint ValidateLocaleAndStoreId(char * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Validates locale string and stores locale ID if valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Convert locale string to locale ID via FUN_00409cc7\n  2. Build locale flag based on g_bCountryIs3Char (0xffff, 0x1002 or 0x0ffe, 0x1002)\n  3. Call g_pfnLocaleHandler with locale ID and flags to validate\n  4. If handler returns 0, clear g_dwLocaleValidation (no error) and return 1\n  5. If handler succeeds (non-zero):\n     - Validate country code via FUN_0040aee0\n     - If country code valid (returns 0):\n       - Call FUN_00409b2a to check codepage (locale + 0x0)\n       - If codepage valid (non-zero):\n         - Set g_dwLocaleValidation bit 2 (0x4)\n         - Store locale ID in g_dwLocaleId and g_wLocaleCodePage\n  6. Return (~g_dwLocaleValidation &gt;&gt; 2) & 1\n\nParameters:\n  pszLocaleString - Locale string to validate\n\nReturns:\n  1 if validation cleared flag (early success path)\n  0 if country code/codepage validation succeeded and flag set\n  1 if validation completed and flag bit 2 is clear\n  Bitwise result of validation state\nlpLocaleEnumProc parameter of EnumSystemLocalesA\n",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:23bf89acf8a4b7c1199669377d8a053ff8cd88f54a878371fce3b0fa3674c05a",
