      "signature": "undefined1 * BuildItemNameString(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined1 *",
      "comment": "Builds a colon-separated string from item name pairs in global table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Access global item table at 0x413198 (contains 8 entry pointers)\n  2. PASS 1 - Calculate total buffer size:\n     For each of 8 items:\n       - Get length of first name (field offset 0x0)\n       - Get length of second name (field offset 0x1C)\n       - Add 2 bytes for separator colons (0x3a ':')\n     Total = sum of all string lengths + 16 separators + 1 null terminator\n  3. Allocate memory block sized (total + 1)\n  4. PASS 2 - Build output string:\n     For each of 8 items:\n       - Write ':' separator (0x3a)\n       - Copy first name using CopyStringWithNullCheck\n       - Write ':' separator (0x3a)\n       - Copy second name using CopyStringWithNullCheck\n     - Append null terminator (0x00)\n  5. Return pointer to allocated buffer\n\nParameters:\n  (implicit) Uses global pointer table at 0x413198\n\nReturns:\n  On success: byte pointer to allocated colon-separated string\n  On failure: NULL if malloc returns NULL at step 3",
