      "name": "CloneStringTableDeep",
      "signature": "undefined4 * CloneStringTableDeep(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4 *",
      "comment": "Deep clones the global string table structure with all embedded strings.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Load global string table pointer from g_pItemNameTable (0x413198)\n    2. Calculate total string buffer size needed:\n       a. Loop 7 (0x7) iterations: sum strlen of string pairs at offsets 0x00 and 0x1C\n          Add 2 bytes per pair for null terminators\n       b. Loop 12 (0xC) iterations: sum strlen of string pairs at offsets 0x38 and 0x68\n          Add 2 bytes per pair for null terminators\n       c. Get strlen of 5 additional strings at offsets 0x98, 0x9C, 0xA0, 0xA4, 0xA8\n    3. Allocate contiguous block: structure size 0xAC (172) + total string length + 5 terminators\n       Total allocation = cbStrings + 0xB1 (177)\n    4. Copy base structure (0xAC bytes) via MoveMemoryOptimized\n    5. Deep copy strings into buffer space after structure:\n       a. Copy 7 string pairs (offsets 0x00/0x1C), update pointers in cloned structure\n       b. Copy 12 string pairs (offsets 0x38/0x68), update pointers in cloned structure\n       c. Copy 5 individual strings (offsets 0x98-0xA8), update pointers\n    6. Return pointer to cloned structure\n\n  Parameters:\n    None - operates on global g_pItemNameTable\n\n  Returns:\n    Pointer to newly allocated deep-cloned structure with all strings\n    NULL if malloc fails\n\n  Structure Layout:\n    Offset | Size | Field              | Type       | Description\n    -------|------|--------------------| -----------|------------------------\n    0x00   | 0x1C | aszFirstNames[7]   | char*[7]   | First string pointers\n    0x1C   | 0x1C | aszSecondNames[7]  | char*[7]   | Second string pointers\n    0x38   | 0x30 | aszThirdGroup[12]  | char*[12]  | Third group string ptrs\n    0x68   | 0x30 | aszFourthGroup[12] | char*[12]  | Fourth group string ptrs\n    0x98   | 0x04 | pszExtra1          | char*      | Extra string 1\n    0x9C   | 0x04 | pszExtra2          | char*      | Extra string 2\n    0xA0   | 0x04 | pszExtra3          | char*      | Extra string 3\n    0xA4   | 0x04 | pszExtra4          | char*      | Extra string 4\n    0xA8   | 0x04 | pszExtra5          | char*      | Extra string 5\n    0xAC   | var  | (string data)      | char[]     | Inline string storage\n\n  Memory Model:\n    - Caller owns returned pointer (must free when done)\n    - Source structure (g_pItemNameTable) is read-only during clone\n    - Strings stored contiguously after structure header for cache efficiency",
