      "name": "DuplicateStringBuffer",
      "signature": "char * DuplicateStringBuffer(char * lpszSource)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Duplicates a null-terminated string by allocating new memory and copying the content.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input string pointer is not NULL\n2. Calculate length of source string using CalculateStringLength\n3. Allocate new buffer with size (length + 1) for null terminator\n4. Validate memory allocation succeeded\n5. Copy source string to new buffer using OptimizedStringCopy\n6. Return pointer to newly allocated string buffer\n\nParameters:\nlpszSource: Pointer to null-terminated source string to duplicate\n\nReturns:\nSuccess: Pointer to newly allocated string buffer containing duplicate\nFailure: NULL if input is NULL or memory allocation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Input NULL: Returns NULL immediately without allocation\n- Allocation failure: Returns NULL, no memory leak as malloc failed\n- Empty string: Allocates 1 byte for null terminator only\n\nError Handling:\n- Input validation: NULL check before processing\n- Memory allocation: Returns NULL on malloc failure\n- No cleanup needed on failure paths",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
