      "name": "GfxSetParameterAndInvoke",
      "signature": "void GfxSetParameterAndInvoke(int nGfxParameter)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets a graphics interface parameter and invokes the corresponding virtual method.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - wraps vtable call at offset 0x58 with parameter setup\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If nGfxParameter is non-zero, store it to g_nGfxInterfaceParameter global\n2. Load g_pGfxInterface pointer (graphics interface vtable)\n3. Load current g_nGfxInterfaceParameter value into ECX\n4. Call virtual method at vtable offset 0x58 with parameter in ECX\n\nParameters:\n  nGfxParameter (int) - Graphics parameter value to set. If zero, uses existing\n                        g_nGfxInterfaceParameter value without modification.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero parameter: Skips parameter update, uses existing global value\n  - Non-zero parameter: Updates global before invoking method\n\nMemory Model:\n  - Reads: g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c), g_nGfxInterfaceParameter (0x6faae19c)\n  - Writes: g_nGfxInterfaceParameter (0x6faae19c) if parameter non-zero\n\nCallers:\n  - InitializeVideoSettings: Sets initial graphics parameter during video init\n\nVirtual Method:\n  - Offset 0x58 in g_pGfxInterface vtable\n  - Parameter passed in ECX (implicit __thiscall-like convention)",
