      "comment": "Initialize the global GameDataCollection object and register error handler.\n\nClassification: Initialization function (thunk wrapper)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pass address of global g_GameDataCollection (0x6fbe9128) to InitializeGameDataCollection via ECX (__fastcall)\n2. Initialize the GameDataCollection structure with embedded objects, vtables, and critical section\n3. Register aterror handler at address 0x6fad8150 via RegisterAterrorHandlerWrapper\n4. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nCalled From:\nReferenced from data pointer at 0x6fbae010 (likely initialization function table)\n\nCallees:\nInitializeGameDataCollection - Constructs GameDataCollection with embedded objects and synchronization\nRegisterAterrorHandlerWrapper - Registers error handler, returns 0 on success or -1 on failure\n\nGlobal Data:\ng_GameDataCollection (0x6fbe9128) - 104-byte GameDataCollection structure with:\n  - vtable pointer, embedded objects, critical section at +0x50\n  - Used for game data management with thread synchronization\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6fbe9128 - Address of global GameDataCollection instance\n0x6fad8150 - Aterror handler function address passed to registration\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThis is a simple initialization wrapper that sets up global game data infrastructure.\nCalled once during module initialization to prepare data structures before game logic runs.",
