      "name": "GfxValidateClipCoordinates",
      "signature": "void GfxValidateClipCoordinates(int nMinX, int nMinY, int nMaxX, int nMaxY, dword dwWidth, dword dwHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates clip coordinates and invokes graphics interface function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if minimum coordinates are within maximum bounds (nMinX <= nMaxX AND nMinY <= nMaxY)\n2. If bounds valid, call graphics interface function (offset +0xB8 from g_pGfxInterface) with dimensions\n3. Otherwise return without calling graphics function (safety check for invalid bounds)\n\nParameters:\n- nMinX (int): Minimum X coordinate\n- nMinY (int): Minimum Y coordinate  \n- nMaxX (int): Maximum X coordinate\n- nMaxY (int): Maximum Y coordinate\n- dwWidth (dword): Width value passed to graphics interface\n- dwHeight (dword): Height value passed to graphics interface\n\nReturns:\n- void",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
