      "name": "GfxResizeWindow",
      "signature": "int GfxResizeWindow(dword dwGameState, int nResolutionMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Resizes the game window to a specified resolution mode.\n\nCalled during game state transitions and after cutscenes to restore proper window dimensions.\nOnly operates in windowed mode (g_dwVideoParam == 1); fullscreen mode skips resize logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate g_pGfxInterface is initialized (assert if NULL)\n2. Early exit with TRUE if nResolutionMode==0 AND dwGameState matches g_dwGameState\n3. Store dwGameState to g_dwGameState global\n4. If not windowed mode (g_dwVideoParam != 1), skip to step 10\n5. Select resolution based on nResolutionMode switch:\n   - Mode 0: 640x480\n   - Mode 1: 800x600\n   - Mode 2: 1344x700\n   - Other: Fatal error with \"Unknown resolution %d\"\n6. Store height to g_dwScreenHeight\n7. Calculate adjusted window rect via AdjustWindowRectEx (WS_POPUP|WS_VISIBLE, WS_EX_APPWINDOW)\n8. Get desktop client rect for centering calculation\n9. Call SetWindowPos to resize and reposition window (SWP_NOCOPYBITS=0x16)\n10. Call graphics interface vtable method +0x24 with dwGameState\n11. Call InitializeVideoSettings to apply changes\n12. Return result from vtable call\n\nParameters:\n  dwGameState - New game state to transition to (stored to g_dwGameState)\n  nResolutionMode - Resolution selection: 0=640x480, 1=800x600, 2=1344x700\n\nReturns:\n  int - TRUE (1) on early exit when state unchanged, otherwise result from vtable call\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_pGfxInterface (0x6fabd21c) - Graphics interface vtable pointer [READ]\n  g_dwGameState (0x6fabd230) - Current game state [READ/WRITE]\n  g_dwVideoParam (0x6fabd22c) - Video mode (1=windowed) [READ]\n  g_dwInitFlag (0x6fabd234) - Window handle (HWND) [READ]\n  g_dwScreenHeight (0x6fabd708) - Screen height [WRITE]\n\nWindows API Calls:\n  AdjustWindowRectEx - Calculate window size from client size\n  GetDesktopWindow - Get desktop window handle\n  GetClientRect - Get desktop dimensions\n  SetWindowPos - Resize and reposition window\n\nError Handling:\n  Asserts if g_pGfxInterface is NULL (line 467 in Window.cpp)\n  Fatal error if nResolutionMode > 2 (\"Unknown resolution %d\")\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1D3 (467) - Assert line number\n  0xC00000 - WS_POPUP | WS_VISIBLE window style\n  0x40000 - WS_EX_APPWINDOW extended style\n  0x16 - SWP_NOCOPYBITS flag for SetWindowPos\n  -2 (0xFFFFFFFE) - HWND_TOP for SetWindowPos",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:78cafc0d373a6eebcb822e5c8d0f6e4f123959ae5f7c84eb237cd3fe3bfb7e9a",
