      "name": "SehExceptionFilter",
      "signature": "dword SehExceptionFilter(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord, void * pContext, dword dwParam3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "SEH exception filter for structured exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if exception flags (ExceptionFlags & 0x66) indicate unwinding\n2. If unwinding in progress, mark context field at offset 0x24 and return success\n3. Otherwise, call FUN_6faa74e9 to process exception with context data\n4. If status field at offset 0x24 remains zero, call SehUnwindHandler\n5. Execute continuation handler at context offset 0x18 and return its result\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionRecord (PEXCEPTION_RECORD): Exception information record\n- pContext (void*): SEH context structure containing handler offsets and state\n- dwParam3 (dword): Additional parameter (purpose undetermined)\n\nReturns:\n- Handler return value from context offset 0x18, typically 0 or 1",
