      "name": "CloseAndCleanupFileStreams",
      "signature": "int CloseAndCleanupFileStreams(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes and cleans up file stream structures during shutdown\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire stream structure table critical section (index 2)\n2. Iterate through stream structure table starting at index 3\n3. For each valid stream structure with flags 0x83 set, close the file\n4. For indices >= 20 (0x14), also delete critical section and deallocate memory\n5. Release critical section and return count of successfully closed files\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Number of files successfully closed (ThreadSafeFileClose returned success)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x2 - Critical section index for stream structure table lock\n0x3 - Starting index for stream iteration (indices 0-2 are reserved)\n0x14 (20) - Threshold index; streams at or above this are deallocated\n0x83 - Flag mask at offset 0xC indicating stream needs closing\n0x20 - Offset to embedded CRITICAL_SECTION within stream structure\n0xFFFFFFFF (-1) - ThreadSafeFileClose failure return value\n\nStructure Layout (Stream Structure):\nOffset  Size  Field               Description\n0x00    4     pFileHandle         File handle or pointer\n0x0C    1     bFlags              Stream state flags (0x83 = needs close)\n0x20    24    criticalSection     Embedded CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Indices 0-2 are reserved and never processed\n- Indices 3-19 have files closed but structures are not deallocated (persistent)\n- Indices 20+ have files closed AND structures fully deallocated (dynamic)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
