      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Returns count of successfully validated context entities\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push constant 1 (Count Mode) as parameter\n2. Call ProcessLockContextEntities with count mode enabled\n3. Clean up stack and return validation count\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Count of successfully validated lock context entities (>= 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if lock context table is empty\n- Returns 0 if no entities pass validation\n\nWrapper Details:\nThis is a convenience wrapper that calls ProcessLockContextEntities(1)\nto perform count mode validation without exposing the mode parameter",
