      "name": "UnlinkListNode",
      "signature": "void UnlinkListNode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unlinks a node from a doubly-linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load node pointer from input parameter (EAX points to list node structure)\n2. If node pointer is null, exit without modification\n3. Load offset value from node+4\n4. If offset is negative, apply NOT operation to convert to pointer address\n5. If offset is positive, calculate previous node by subtracting previous's next offset\n6. Update previous node's forward pointer to current node's value\n7. Update next node's back pointer with current node's next value\n8. Clear current node's forward pointer (set to null)\n9. Clear current node's back pointer (set to null)\n\nParameters:\n  pListNode (EAX): Pointer to doubly-linked list node at offset +0 (points to previous)\n                   and offset +4 (signed offset/pointer to next)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Negative offset values indicate direct pointer references (bitwise NOT applied)\n  - Positive offset values use offset-based calculation: current - (next offset - previous offset)\n  - Null node pointers result in no operation\n  - Offset value at [node+4] can represent either: direct pointer (~value) or offset distance",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c22772dbf9d7cd755f9fde1dd64bf6b2da2a0cb384a854b18d8978907feeea80",
